uration**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the server setup. The `package.json` reveals a `server.ts` file and a `tsx server.ts` start script. This contrasts with the system instructions\' preference for `node server.ts`. I need to ensure `tsx` is correctly installed. I am examining the discrepancy, considering implications for video transcription. This `server.ts` file needs to work correctly.\n\n\n**Clarifying Video Transcription**\n\nI\'m now clarifying the approach to video transcription. Calling the Gemini API from the client is out. The guidelines mandate real integrations, not mocks, for user data. I\'ve realized Gemini can transcribe audio/video directly. The key is how to handle the upload. I\'m exploring server-side processing using Express and Node. I need to figure out upload size limits. Does the server send the file to Gemini or extract the audio? I can play the uploaded video in the browser!\n\n\n"
