  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Request**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the core of this request. My primary objective is a deep dive into the \"Bento Grid\" design. I need to dissect the styling elements and layout structures from the given HTML. I\'ll isolate colors, fonts, spacing, borders, shadows, backgrounds, and gradients, as well as the flexbox/grid architecture and component arrangement. My goal is to extract *only* that styling.\n\n\n**Refining the Approach**\n\nI\'m now integrating the design specifics. The instructions highlight preserving existing HTML structure. I\'m focusing on CSS modifications. I\'ve begun extracting color values from the HTML design, noting the dark `#020617` background, the slate/white text pairings, and the blue accents for headers/logos. I\'m analyzing the Bento card styling, including the `rgba` backgrounds, borders, `border-radius`, and flexbox structure. The timeline block\'s attributes are also under consideration.\n\n\n**Deconstructing the Grid**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in the grid layout, focusing on the Bento HTML structure. I\'ve noted the 12-column grid and the row spans of the cards within the `main` container, specifically the `col-span` and `row-span` attributes of each. I\'m taking the time to extract the dimensions of the video preview card (8/12 cols, 4/6 rows) and the placement of the smaller card blocks at the bottom.\n\n\n**Mapping the Components**\n\nI\'m now mapping the specific components within the Bento grid. I\'ve noted the `col-span-4 row-span-5` for the transcript editor, the bottom timeline\'s `col-span-12 row-span-1`. My understanding is that it\'s a 12-column grid, with the video previewer spanning 8 columns and 4 rows. The sidebar editor spans 4 columns and 5 rows. I\'m focusing on adapting the Bento structure, while maintaining our existing tabs and controls, like the deep dark slate background.\n\n\n"
