ntaining brand consistency. Additionally, I\'m dynamically displaying the current project file name, using a placeholder if none is uploaded. The text formatting mirrors the Bento Grid\'s visual style, enhancing seamless theme integration.\n\n\n**Adjusting Bento Styling**\n\nI\'m now incorporating Bento card styles. For the video player, I\'m updating the container with `bg-black/60`, `backdrop-blur-md`, and a subtle border. The interactive subtitle track container is getting similar treatment with `bg-[#0f172a]/60` and blur to match the aesthetic.\n\n\n**Adding Waveform Bars**\n\nI\'m now incorporating waveform bars into the timeline\'s background. I\'m focusing on rendering a full grid of bars within the container, aiming for an elegant wave shape or high-quality layout. I\'m tweaking the height and spacing parameters to optimize visual appeal.\n\n\n**Optimizing Waveform Display**\n\nI\'m now implementing the waveform bar generation with the provided heights, ensuring dynamic pulsing during playback with the `Math.sin` function. I\'m focusing on the `className` for the bars, applying `bg-[#475569]` color and `rounded-sm`. I\'m using `transition-all duration-300` and `minHeight: \'4px\'` to match a high-tech Bento aesthetic. I\'m making sure to address the code and implementation of the bars with `height` styles dependent on `baseHeight`.\n\n\n\n**Refining Right Column Styles**\n\nI\'m now focusing on refining the Right Column\'s styling to match the Bento aesthetic. I\'ve updated the container with `bg-[#0f172a]/45`, `backdrop-blur-md`, and a border. The tab selections are now styled with `bg-[#0c1322]/80`. Next I\'ll be reviewing the styles of the individual buttons inside the tabs!\n\n\n**Improving Tab Button Styling**\n\nI\'m now refining the tab button\'s look for the Bento aesthetic. The active state will feature a more refined appearance with `border-blue-500 text-blue-400 bg-slate-900/40 backdrop-blur`. I\'m going through the style settings for the inner components of the tabs, like the quick presets, and tweaking them accordingly. The quick presets will now have a rounded appearance!\n\n\n**Adjusting Input Styles**\n\nI\'m now focusing on refining the styling of input elements within the Bento aesthetic. I\'m updating input and select elements with a high-tech Bento styling, aiming for a consistent visual language. For example, inputs are getting `bg-[#1e293b]/60 border border-slate-700/80` and rounded corners to match other styled components. I\'m making sure all inputs look like a unified high-tech theme.\n\n\n"
