  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Crafting A Concise Response**\n\nThe compilation is successful! I\'m now structuring a concise and helpful response for the user, addressing their questions about the Android app\'s completion and testing procedures. I\'m focusing on professionalism and clarity.\n\n\n**Describing Visual Aspects**\n\nI\'m now detailing the visual elements. I\'m noting the branding (CaptionFlow Mobile), dynamic connection status, and key sections like the header zone. I\'m also planning to emphasize the matching preview mode in the web workbench. I am confident I\'ll convey the app\'s look and feel accurately.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I have successfully completed the core setup for the Android app. Below is an overview of how the **CaptionFlow Mobile** experience looks and how you can run and test it.\n\n---\n\n### 1. How the Android Companion App Looks & Behaves\nThe interface has been meticulously structured using **Jetpack Compose** (Android\'s flagship modern UI toolkit) to mirror the elite style of the web studio. Here is what the app workspace includes:\n\n*   **Header Zone**: Branded head bar featuring `\"CaptionFlow Mobile // Companion Sync Studio\"`. It sports a live green `\"Dev Local Link\"` status badge indicating connection readiness.\n*   **Media Sandbox / Waveforms**: A widescreen viewport showing subtitle overlays synchronized in real-time. Underneath the subtitles, a multi-band simulated audio visualizer bounces dynamically during playback.\n*   **Precision Scrubbing**: Fluid play/pause controls paired with a dragging seek slider allowing you to step frame-by-frame through the caption track.\n*   **Workspace Drawers (Tabs)**:\n    *   *Timelines*: Lists all current caption markers with speaker name, times, and text. The active line turns deep slate-blue with a glowing outline to matching the current video playhead.\n    *   *Aesthetic Presets Row*: One-tap layout preset switchers like **Karaoke Highlight** (amber text + monospace fonts), **Speaker Accent** (blue text), and **Classic Slate**.\n    *   *Add Subtitle Panel*: A secondary view with numeric text inputs to inject, edit, or adjust times on the fly.\n*   **Exporter Controls**: Fast exporting commands to output compliant `.srt`, `.vtt`, or plain `.txt` files directly onto your device storage.\n\n---\n\n### 2. How to Compile, Build, and Test the Android App\nBecause we are in a web development container, you can test and compile the Android app by using the following methods:\n\n#### Method A: Open and Run in Android Studio (Recommended for actual devices)\n1. **Download Code**: Export/download this workspace as a ZIP archive using the platform settings.\n2. **Import Project**: Unzip the folder and open it inside **Android Studio** (Koala or newer recommended).\n3. **Run on Emulator / Phone**: Ensure you have virtual devices (AVD) set up, or plug your physical Android phone in with **USB Debugging** enabled. Click the green **Run** button (`Shift + F10`) inside Android Studio.\n4. Android Studio will automatically build the APK using the compiled Gradle configurations (`build.gradle.kts`) and boot CaptionFlow Mobile.\n\n#### Method B: Command Line Build (Produces the debug APK)\nIf you have the Android SDK installed locally, you can navigate inside the workspace and build an installable APK using Gradle commands:\n```bash\n./gradlew assembleDebug\n```\nThe compiled APK will be outputted under: \n`app/build/outputs/apk/debug/app-debug.apk` \n\n---\n\n### 3. Immediate Testing in Web Sandbox\nIf you want to play with the logic immediately without compiling locally, our web workbench running in your preview browser includes a **Codec Simulation / Subtitle playhead engine**. Simply click the **Play** button on any preset video card in the web app\342\200\224if your browser blocks raw MP4 native codecs, the system seamlessly triggers the **Interactive Simulator Mode** which lets you experience the real-time caption animations, seeking tracks, and active visualizer just as it functions on Android!"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 2
      nanos: 945973184
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
